# It keeps going: the pages for what stays across turns (PLAN-catalogue.md). `changes` and `back` take several turns and keep them in the table (`turns`).
# Undo is a tap on a chip and the language view is a tap on a button, so neither has a page here.

# changes: the boat is drawn once; asking for a bigger sail sends one line, and nothing else is redrawn.
scene changes figure lines=1 brisk
look paper
line sea 0,70 160,70 thick=1
poly hull @with 50,60 110,60 100,72 60,72 fill=ink
rect mast @with 78,26 2x34 fill=ink
poly sail @with 80,28 80,56 104,56 fill=accent
wait 0.47s

# back: a moon and a tree, then a house; the turns after this one are in the table.
scene back figure brisk
look paper
circle moon1 40,30 12 fill=accent stroke=none
rect trunk1 @with 108,50 6x30 fill=ink
circle crown1 @with 111,42 16 fill=alt stroke=none
wait 0.5s
